\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jerusalem, my happy home,
\par When shall I come to thee?
\par When shall my sorrows have 
\par an end?
\par Thy joys when shall I see?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O happy harbour of the saints!
\par O sweet and pleasant soil!
\par In thee no sorrow may be found,
\par No grief, no care, no toil.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy walls are made of precious stones,
\par Thy bulwarks diamonds square;
\par Thy gates are of right orient pearl,
\par Exceeding rich and rare.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy turrets and thy pinnacles
\par With carbunicles do shine
\par Thy very streets are paved with gold
\par Surpassing clear and fine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy vineyards and thy orchards are
\par Most beautiful and fair,
\par Full furnished with trees and fruits
\par Most wonderful and rare.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thy gardens and thy gallant walks
\par Continually are green,
\par There grow such sweet and pleasant 
\par flowers
\par As nowhere else are seen.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Quite through the streets with
\par silver sound,
\par The flood of life doth flow;
\par Upon whose banks on every side
\par The wood of life doth grow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Thy saints are crowned with glory
\par great,
\par They see God face to face;
\par They triumph still, they still rejoice,
\par Most happy is their case.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 9. There David stands with harp
\par in hand
\par As master of the quire,
\par Ten thousand times that man
\par were blest
\par That might this music hear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. There Magdalene hath left her moan,
\par And cheerfully doth sing,
\par With blessed Saints, whose harmony
\par In every street doth ring.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. Jerusalem, Jerusalem,
\par God grant me once to see
\par Thy endless joys, and of the same
\par Partaker aye to be.
\par                       Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

